  "page": null,
  "source": "[\\derivative:of{f}:at{x0}]\nDefines: d is \\real\nwhen:\n. x0 is \\\\anything\n. f is \\\\anything\nexpresses:\n. forAll: eps is \\real\n  where: eps \\:real.greater?:/ \\real.zero\n  then:\n  . exists: delta is \\real\n    suchThat:\n    . delta \\:real.greater?:/ \\real.zero\n    . forAll: h is \\real\n      where:\n      . h != \\real.zero\n      . \\real.abs(h) \\:real.less?:/ delta\n      then: \\real.abs(((f(x0 \\.real.+./ h) \\.real.-./ f(x0)) \\.real.div./ h) \\.real.-./ d) \\:real.less?:/ eps\nDocumented:\n. called: \"derivative of $f?$ at $x0?$\"\n. written: \"f?'(x0?)\"\n. description: \"The derivative\n                $f'(x_0) = \\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{f(x_0 + h) - f(x_0)}{h}$.\"\nId: \"a8704cca-424a-4f17-a321-d5c3725e2090\"",
